  "rationale": "No research-backed structural redesign converts the externally controlled, qualification-fragmented service mechanism into an obtainable founder-controlled control point with demonstrated fully loaded economics. Removing capacity reservations would collapse the offer into the documented incumbent's nonexclusive spot-dispatch model, while retaining or strengthening reservations still lacks any signed technician commitment, unrelated-installer prepayment, workable cross-brand data and OEM rights, or contribution evidence. A direct-owner subscription would instead confront an existing substitute whose remote triage can reduce field-dispatch demand. The evidence supports bounded validation experiments, but not a changed structure that can honestly claim different control and economics.",
